//- The side panel's fixed part — what does not depend on the site's contents.
//-
//- It is drawn the moment the page is (frame.pug), so the content never moves
//- when the rest arrives; static/js/site.js fills it from nav.json:
//-   * "Contents" — the pages in the menu (`hidden` unset), grouped by their
//-     top-level folder, before the filter, when the site has any;
//-   * the filter inside `details.side-fold` (owner, 2026-09-26: "tag area and
//-     selection should be done on the side panel, also search should be
//-     there"): a search box — a GET form to the folio list — and the areas
//-     with their counts, the current folio's area marked.
//- No tags here (owner, 2026-09-29: "tags on the side bar are broken, remove
//- them from sidebar") — a folio's tags are its chip bar below the content.
//- `contents` on the fold too: it folds on a phone like the contents do.
nav.site-nav
  h2.intro #[a(href="/") folio]
  p.tagline one subject, one A4 page
  details.contents.side-fold(open)
    summary
      span.contents-label.side-fold-label Filter
      svg.chevron(viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true")
        path(d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round")
